  "title": "Where the chances really were",
  "lead": "A summary of the lotteries over five years, from 2021 to 2025. It shows how many applications there were per apartment in each city.",
  "explain": "This is the one thing you can influence. Eligibility, the number of apartments and the draw date are not yours to choose — but the city is. The difference between cities is enormous.",
  "caution": "One family applies to several projects at once, so this is not “that many families per place” but a load indicator. And it is not a forecast: each lottery has its own set of cities and terms. But the order of magnitude repeats from year to year.",
